    "narrative": "With the 2026 season nearing its conclusion, the Austin Waves offense centers around two elite anchors today: **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Kyle Tucker** (80.37). **Gunnar Henderson** holds our highest efficiency score, benefiting from a prime matchup against Elmer Rodr\u00edguez; the 5.31 xERA suggests a volatile environment that favors **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s elite power-speed profile, even with the wind-in penalty at the stadium. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** remains a must-start against Seymour. While the park factors slightly dampen his output, the combination of a high-xERA pitcher and the wind blowing out significantly inflates his potential for extra-base hits, solidifying his role as our primary outfielder. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.08) also earns strong consideration, as his platoon advantage against Baz provides a high-floor opportunity to accumulate counting stats in the middle of the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup optimization involved **Liam Hicks** (39.98). He narrowly missed the starting cut, as the optimizer prioritized the defensive stability and positional versatility of our current MI/UTIL slots. **Liam Hicks** was penalized by the assignment of facing Zack Wheeler, whose 3.16 xERA represents a \"tough arm\" threshold that suppresses overall efficiency scores, regardless of the individual hitter's talent. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Drake Baldwin**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Andy Pages**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Dominic Smith**; their scores are currently pegged to assumed batting positions. Should **Nasim Nunez** or **Brayan Rocchio** drop further down the order, we may need to adjust to protect our daily game cap efficiency, especially given **Nasim Nunez**\u2019s role as a primary stolen base threat who remains vulnerable to the 3.86 xERA of Manaea. We continue to manage the health of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jackson Merrill** closely, keeping them sidelined as we navigate the final stretch of this Roto campaign.",
